{"title":"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the second smallest positive integer that is divisible by every positive integer less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b8baf686a05f9e90813cb4adc33ae41213db8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must be divisible by every positive integer less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d87c4f20da2e1950da5c2d2b8fcebab09cb12b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4, 5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Each number that is divisible by each of these is a multiple of their least common multiple. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13d80a26e067a91b0f6607a802dd6123e4c4fcd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LCM(1,2,3,4,5,6)=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />, so each number divisible by these is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The smallest multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the second smallest multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/9/d994ac6816732e38036acb22c1590134da24bba9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\times60=120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57b5b60125e1aa4292d3623765b3b4882ef23eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+0=\\boxed{3\\ \\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"151\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B\">2011 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1